{"kind":"report","text":"approved at d4726958c7d3fc763e734e43b42be0da40e2daa3 (SKILL.md,\ndocs/reference/architecture.md, AGENTS.md).\n\nSecond review, on the repair of changes-requested verdict 7d3ef0e5. Reviewed\nin the clean checkout at /Users/hughpyle/play/gitseq-worktrees/skill-simplify\nat the exact head. `git diff 3049d18b..d4726958` touches SKILL.md and\ndocs/reference/architecture.md only; `git diff main..d4726958` touches those\ntwo and AGENTS.md. No Go file differs from main, so every source line number I\nverified in the first round still stands at this head.\n\nThe artifact set is right: three artifacts, one per path the head changes\nagainst main, all at d4726958, all effective, all on promise 75575b56, each\nresting on the promise and the same eleven behaviour bases. 76fa1b66 at\nSKILL.md is the reporting artifact and is sequenced last.\n\nAll three blocking findings are repaired. I checked each against the code and\nthe pages rather than against the implementer's account, and I re-derived the\ncorrected citations myself.\n\n## Architecture\n\nAffected layer: layer 7, \"CLI, MCP, skills, connectors, and UI\" — the\n`AGENTS.md` and `SKILL.md` rows of the package-boundary table and the \"Review\nrule\" section of docs/reference/architecture.md. This head changes that\ncontract and now records the change in the same head, with its artifact\nde041a56 published at docs/reference/architecture.md. That satisfies the rule\nthe page states about itself at :2769-2772, which is what blocked the first\nround.\n\nThe rewrite is accurate against the tree:\n\n- :2747, the AGENTS.md row, now says that page carries what this repository\n  adds on top of SKILL.md and names the rules it deliberately repeats, and\n  that the three review conclusions live in SKILL.md. AGENTS.md at this head\n  is 40 lines: three deliberately repeated rules at :20-23, the\n  superseded-world merge refusal at :25-28, the dot-artifact migration at\n  :30-34, and presence at :36-40. Nothing else. The row describes it exactly.\n- :2748, the SKILL.md row, now names the three conclusions. They are at\n  SKILL.md:123-136.\n- :2772-2776, the Review rule, no longer attributes the security and\n  simplification checks to AGENTS.md and no longer says SKILL.md does not\n  carry repository policies. The reviewer-must-request-changes sentence at\n  :2769-2772 is untouched, which is right — that rule was not the defect.\n\nI checked the whole page rather than only the two places I named, as asked.\nEvery mention of either file is at :1485, :2433, :2747, :2748 and :2772-2776.\nThe two I did not flag are still true: :1485 (\"the agent practice in\n`SKILL.md`\") and :2433 (\"`SKILL.md` is the normative operating contract for an\nagent participating in the Workroom application\"), which if anything reads\nmore accurately now. No other sentence on the page turns false.\n\nI also swept the rest of the repository for statements about the division of\nthese two files. docs/README.md:130, docs/concepts/components.md:44 and :175,\ndocs/concepts/agent-practice.md:12 and :163, docs/concepts/record.md:52,\ndocs/concepts/work-loop.md:49, docs/how-to/configure-an-agent.md:104 and\nREADME.md:81 all describe SKILL.md as the normative agent contract and remain\ntrue. One cross-reference does not — see Simplification 1; it is not blocking.\n\nThe head preserves every other layer contract. Layers 1 to 6 are untouched.\n\n## Security\n\nBoundary: the signing boundary's dead-basis judgement in\ninternal/app/admission.go, and the authority-bearing request chain the page\nrequires a reviewer to confirm at SKILL.md:131-134. No secrets, no untrusted\ninput, no bounds moved. The defect was that the page licensed an actor to do\nwhat the boundary refuses. It no longer does.\n\nSKILL.md:188-192 now reads: a stale basis is admitted and recorded, so\nre-anchor and carry on rather than stall over it; a retired one refuses, so\nrepoint it before you file; between two the boundary would both admit,